# A flight plan that ends in a landing: the Cessna from over Chatswood, down
# the extended centreline of Sydney airport's 16R, landed on it - by the
# landing learnt by reinforcement learning, which the AI hands her to at its
# gate two miles out, where the aircraft has one, and by the approach
# autopilot otherwise.
#
#   aircraft NAME
#   start LATITUDE LONGITUDE ALTITUDE_FT HEADING_DEG AIRSPEED_KT     in the air
#   waypoint NAME LATITUDE LONGITUDE ALTITUDE_FT AIRSPEED_KT
#   land NAME LATITUDE LONGITUDE ELEVATION_FT HEADING_DEG LENGTH_M
#
# Degrees are WGS84's, altitudes above sea level, airspeeds calibrated. The
# runway is 16R's landing threshold and its true heading and length, from
# assets/runways/strips.csv (OurAirports); the server takes the threshold's
# elevation from the ground it collides on. After the last waypoint the AI
# flies to six and then four miles out on the centreline, on the glidepath,
# and down it (src/sim/plan.hpp).

aircraft c172p
start -33.75045 151.12585 2500 168 90

waypoint CENTRELINE_8NM -33.79925 151.13843 2200 80
land YSSY_16R -33.929401 151.171997 8 167.9 3962
